  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Projet d&#x2019;appui en intrants agricoles aux m&#xE9;nages affect&#xE9;s par les al&#xE9;as climatiques et autres chocs.</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The main objective of this project is to provide life-saving agricultural livelihood assistance to internally displaced persons, returnees and host community members in Kirundo and Muyinga. This FAO project provides agricultural inputs including seeds, fertilizer, tools and livestock feed to farmer households. Additionally the project provides $502,000 in conditional voucher assistance to farmers in need. The project provides humanitarian assistance to 38,600 people, including 9,900 women, 9,400 men, 19,300 children, and including 5,800 persons with disabilities.</narrative>
  </description>
